{"availability":"available","full":"brianphu2310/AML-CTF_Analyst","name":"AML-CTF_Analyst","description":"AML/CTF compliance suite for an Australian law firm: client risk rating, transaction monitoring, alert triage, SMR drafts, and a polite UN sanctions list scraper with name screening. Python, Streamlit. Tests + CI.","category":"Finance","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-10T03:02:33Z","updated":"2026-10-06T10:20:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://aml-ctfanalyst-ewy8ksvvc2qzujnxkcradq.streamlit.app/","topics":["anti-money-laundering","databricks","law","law-firm","legal-tech","python","sql","streamlit"],"demo":"https://aml-ctfanalyst-ewy8ksvvc2qzujnxkcradq.streamlit.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T16:52:59.077Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T16:52:59.077Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T16:52:59.077Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T08:00:51.559Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T16:52:59.077Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["▶ Live demo · Methodology · Simulator · Architecture","An interactive AML/CTF back-office dashboard for a fictional three-office law firm, built as the companion to the firm's financial operations dashboard — same firm, same partners, this time covering client risk rating, transaction monitoring, alert triage, suspicious matter reporting and beneficial-ownership review.","Why this exists: from 1 July 2026, Australia's AML/CTF Tranche 2 reforms bring law firms, accountants and trust and company service providers into the regime as reporting entities for the first time. A firm that has never had to run customer due diligence, transaction monitoring or suspicious matter reporting (SMR) at scale now has to build that function from nothing. This project is what the operational tooling behind that function could look like."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brianphu2310/AML-CTF_Analyst